    "updated_at": "2025-01-28T16:43:17Z",
    "body": "- [dynamically setting `src` on an iframe](https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/13445)\r\n  - Safari: no `load` event when setting `src`.\r\n  - Chrome: fires a `load` event when setting `src`\r\n- [dynamically setting `src` on a lazy-loading hidden `iframe`](https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/13446)\r\n  - Safari: fires a `load` event\r\n  - Chrome: fires a `load` event\r\n\r\nI suppose the PR matches Chrome in that a `load` event is fired for a `javascript:` URL in the `src` attribute unconditionally, but like Safari to evaluate the `javascript:` URL lazily for `loading=lazy` iframes.",
